  "findings": [
    "Employee Voice routes require employee auth and call Copilot; candidate must use interview-scoped endpoints and the existing candidate cookie.",
    "Reuse/extract peer, track, channel, cleanup and SDK primitives; do not mount employee hook/routes on candidate pages or create a second independent WebRTC stack.",
    "Employee response.done is generation completion, not the interview's playback-finished gate. Provider output drain plus verified supported sink semantics require a 5B-0 spike.",
    "Ephemeral secrets can create more than one session until expiry and configuration can be overridden; choose unified server-created call identity and trusted sideband for initial interview design.",
    "Dictation script-dominance filtering exists separately; Realtime uses UI language hints and echo heuristics. Candidate mixed mode must not inherit those rejection/normalization policies.",
    "Existing 700ms provider VAD and engine speech/finalization semantics require an explicit tested turn mapping; no unreviewed aggregation or engine semantic change.",
    "Real mode needs durable connection-generation, item/turn and response/playback fencing, effect dispatch and media-liveness-aware recovery.",
    "Keep MockRealtimeProvider, MockEvaluator and Phase 4 frozen-input/evidence/review path unchanged; no real model or automatic hiring."
  ],
